  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under the current financial resources measurement focus, governmental fund statements recognize the $400,000 premium as an other financing source, a current-period inflow increasing fund balance. Under the economic resources focus in government-wide statements (GASB 34), the full $10.4 million is reported as a long-term liability and the premium is amortized as a reduction of interest expense.
Wrong (B): Bond premiums are classified as other financing sources in governmental accounting, not revenue. Revenue and other financing sources are distinct categories.
Wrong (C): This reverses the treatment. Fund statements do not report long-term liabilities; government-wide statements do.
