-- Q737: State and Local Government Reporting [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["All governmental funds regardless of whether they have a legally adopted budget","The general fund and each major special revenue fund with a legally adopted budget","Enterprise funds and internal service funds that receive appropriations","All funds receiving federal grant funding subject to single audit requirements"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): GASB requires budgetary comparison schedules as RSI for the general fund and each major special revenue fund that has a legally adopted annual budget. These schedules compare original budget, final amended budget, and actual results on the budgetary basis.
Wrong (A): Not all governmental funds require budgetary comparison schedules. Only those meeting both the major fund criterion and the legally adopted budget criterion qualify.
Wrong (C): Enterprise and internal service funds are proprietary funds and are not subject to the budgetary comparison RSI requirement under GASB standards.
Wrong (D): Federal grant funding does not determine the RSI requirement. The criteria are major fund status and having a legally adopted annual budget.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 737;

-- Q738: State and Local Government Reporting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both are reported identically in both statements because GASB 34 harmonized measurement focuses","Both are fund expenditures totaling $350,000; government-wide capitalizes the vehicle and reduces debt","The vehicle is capitalized at the fund level and the debt payment is expensed at government-wide","Both reduce cash equally and the measurement focus only affects classification labels used"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the current financial resources focus, both the $200,000 vehicle purchase and $150,000 debt payment are expenditures reducing fund balance. Under the economic resources focus (government-wide), the vehicle is capitalized as a $200,000 asset and the debt payment reduces bonds payable by $150,000 with no expense recorded.
Wrong (A): GASB 34 intentionally maintains different measurement focuses to serve different reporting objectives. The two sets of statements are not harmonized.
Wrong (C): This reverses the treatment. Fund statements expense both items; government-wide statements capitalize the vehicle and reduce the liability.
Wrong (D): The measurement focus changes both the amounts reported and their classifications, not just labels. A $350,000 expenditure versus a capital asset and liability reduction are substantively different.$EXPL$
