-- Q1094: Pension and Postretirement Benefits [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The corridor is $600,000 (10% of $6M plan assets); the $150,000 excess is amortized at $15,000/year","The full $750,000 is amortized over 10 years at $75,000 per year regardless of corridor threshold","No amortization is required because $750,000 is less than both PBO and plan asset totals","The corridor equals $750,000, so the excess is $0 and no amortization occurs this period"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 715, the corridor is 10% of the greater of PBO ($5,500,000) or plan assets ($6,000,000), which is $600,000. Cumulative losses of $750,000 exceed the corridor by $150,000, amortized over the 10-year average remaining service period at $15,000 per year. The corridor mechanism treats moderate fluctuations as normal estimation noise.
Wrong (B): The corridor approach specifically exempts actuarial amounts below the threshold from amortization. Only the excess over 10% of the greater of PBO or plan assets is amortized.
Wrong (C): The comparison is between cumulative losses and 10% of PBO or plan assets, not the full PBO or plan asset amounts. $750,000 exceeds the $600,000 corridor.
Wrong (D): The corridor is calculated as 10% of the greater of PBO or plan assets ($600,000), not set equal to the cumulative loss amount.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1094;

-- Q1186: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The difference is an accounting error that should be corrected by adjusting fund balance","Funds exclude long-term items; the reconciliation adds capital assets and subtracts long-term debt","Government-wide statements are less accurate because they include estimated long-term values","Fund balance is always higher than net position because funds report all assets comprehensively"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 34, governmental funds use the current financial resources focus, excluding capital assets and long-term liabilities. Government-wide statements use the economic resources focus, including all assets and liabilities. The reconciliation adds capital assets ($45M), subtracts long-term debt ($28M), and adds internal service fund net position ($1.2M) to bridge the gap.
Wrong (A): The difference is not an error but an intentional design feature of dual-perspective reporting under GASB 34. Each measurement focus serves a distinct purpose.
Wrong (C): Government-wide statements provide a broader perspective, not a less accurate one. Including capital assets and long-term obligations gives a more complete picture of financial position.
Wrong (D): Net position is typically higher than fund balance when capital assets exceed long-term debt, which is the reverse of this claim.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1186;

